      "sourceTextSha256": "cd82198f9837ba78bc70f1b3391dcec2cc29b40655c8d1f0f9d8cfbc2084698a",
      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel. At 09:00, the Lima city tour begins, including a visit to Casa de Aliaga.\n\nStart in Miraflores with a visit to Parque del Amor, a view of the Huaca Pucllana archaeological complex from a lookout, and a walk through the Olive Grove Park. Colonial mansions still line the district’s streets.\n\nIn the historic centre, the tour passes through Plaza Mayor. Here you will see the Cathedral, the Presidential Palace and City Hall. The tour also includes the Monastery and Church of San Francisco.\n\nStep inside Casa de Aliaga, a historic private residence. Its story here begins in 1536, when the mansion was built for Jerónimo de Aliaga, an associate of Francisco Pizarro, on the site of a pre-Columbian structure. The same family has owned the house for almost five centuries. Its interiors, antique furniture and artworks offer a glimpse of how the Spanish aristocracy lived in colonial Peru.\n\nAfter the tour, transfer to the airport for your flight to Cusco, the former Inca capital. On arrival, you will be met and transferred to the four-star Xima Cusco hotel or similar.",
